  "solution": {
    "text": "By superposition principle,\n\\(\\mathrm{v}_{1}=\\frac{-\\mathrm{GM}}{2 \\mathrm{R}^{3}}\\left[3 \\mathrm{R}^{2}-\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{R}}{2}\\right)^{2}\\right]\\)\n\\(=-\\frac{11 \\mathrm{GM}}{8 \\mathrm{R}^{3}}\\)\nAlso, \\(\\mathrm{v}_{2}=-\\frac{3}{2} \\frac{\\mathrm{G}(\\mathrm{M} / 8)}{(\\mathrm{R} / 2)}=\\frac{-3 \\mathrm{GM}}{8 \\mathrm{R}}\\)\nThe required potential is, \\(\\mathrm{v}=\\mathrm{v}_{1}-\\mathrm{v}_{2}\\)\n\\(\\begin{array}{l}\n=-\\frac{11 \\mathrm{GM}}{8 \\mathrm{R}}-\\left(-\\frac{3 \\mathrm{GM}}{8 \\mathrm{R}}\\right) \\\\\n\\mathrm{V}=-\\frac{\\mathrm{GM}}{\\mathrm{R}}\n\\end{array}\\)"
